# Meathook Massacre II's "return that card" is about the card the creature became in its owner's graveyard (CR 400.7): if it
# has left the graveyard before the ability resolves, it is a new object and isn't returned. Bot1 casts Meathook Massacre II
# for X = 1 and sacrifices its only creature, a Memnite. With the death trigger on the stack Bot1 casts Cling to Dust on that
# Memnite (exiled, 3 life gained). The trigger then resolves: Bot1 may still pay 3 life and does (the life is paid as the
# ability resolves, the rulings), but the Memnite stays in exile.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Memnite
Meathook Massacre II
Swamp
Cling to Dust
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x27

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Meathook Massacre II.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard.Memnite.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cling to Dust.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Life = 23
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Exile = Memnite
Bot1.Exile.Memnite.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Meathook Massacre II; Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Mox Ruby; Swamp
Bot1.Graveyard = Cling to Dust; Black Lotus
